<title>USA: TABLE - PP&amp;L Resources Q2 shr $0.39 lower.</title>
<headline>TABLE - PP&amp;L Resources Q2 shr $0.39 lower.</headline>
<dateline>ALLENTOWN, Pa 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.39		    $0.38</p>
<p> Net			 64,553		   61,327</p>
<p> Oper revs		686,009		  669,070</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 164,068		  160,610</p>
<p>	  6  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.11		    $1.11</p>
<p> Net			181,325		  177,589</p>
<p> Oper revs	    1,471,778		1,458,263</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 163,660		  160,271</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Full company name is PP&amp;L Resources Inc.</p>
<p>The company said it will record a one-time transaction cost of $0.06 a share in the third quarter due to its recently announced acquisition of Penn Fuel Gas Co.</p>
<p>It said it could also take a charge of $0.24 a share in the same quarter if the new British government brings into law a proposed windfall profits tax on privatized regional electric companies.</p>
